---
description: Agent surface, memory, and repo-scoped MCP maintenance
globs: ["AGENTS.md", "CLAUDE.md", ".agents/**", ".codex/**", ".cursor/rules/**"]
---

## Scope

Use this rule when changing repo instructions, skills, sub-agent cards, Codex config, MCP declarations, or memory handoff notes.

## Source Placement

- `AGENTS.md`: compact operating contract.
- `CLAUDE.md`: full onboarding, lessons learned, and longer workflow explanations.
- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`: Cursor/editor rules with valid YAML frontmatter.
- `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md`: task workflows; frontmatter must be valid YAML.
- `.codex/agents/*.toml`: repo-local sub-agent role cards.
- `.codex/config.toml`: runtime config only; no `[instructions]` or `developer_instructions`.

## Codex + Cursor Surface Sync

- Keep the Codex-managed/Cursor-implemented workflow synchronized in `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursor/rules/codex-cursor-handoff.mdc`, `.agents/skills/xhverse-dev/SKILL.md`, and relevant `.codex/agents/*.toml`.
- Use `.tmp/*-handoff.md` as the shared instruction surface between Codex and Cursor.
- Codex does not operate Cursor through Computer Use for this repo; Codex prepares handoffs, the user runs Cursor Agent locally, and Cursor writes `.tmp/*-cursor-result.md` for review context.
- Temporary Cursor handoff/result files should be removed after accepted implementation evidence is captured in the final response or durable docs.
- Do not put this workflow into `.codex/config.toml`; that file remains runtime config only.
- Keep implementation-lane defaults synchronized when they change: `codex-spark` first for bounded code implementation, with escalation to the smarter Codex lane when Spark is buggy, misses repo rules, is not production-grade, or the work is high-risk/complex.
- Keep engineering skill defaults synchronized when they change: `debug-mantra` for debugging, `scrutinize` for reviews, and `post-mortem` for validated post-fix writeups.
- Keep content-writing defaults synchronized when they change: `technical_writer` for new content starts and pre-publish content QA, paired with `blog-content-strategy` and `document-writer` for blog work.

## Memory Updates

- Update memory only when the user explicitly asks for memory changes.
- Add a small note under `/Users/bossruji/.codex/memories/extensions/ad_hoc/notes/`.
- Do not edit the generated memory registry directly.

## Repo-Scoped MCP Rules

- Keep xhverse MCPs repo-scoped in `.codex/config.toml`.
- Store only environment variable names, never bearer token values.
- Cloudflare is the default MCP for this repo.
- Supabase tooling is allowed for explicit backend/data/RLS work.
- Do not add Notion for xhverse.
- Remove MCPs that are slow, broken, unused, or not clearly tied to this project.

## Validation

- Parse TOML after `.codex/config.toml` edits.
- Validate skill frontmatter YAML after `SKILL.md` edits.
- Validate Cursor rule frontmatter after `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` edits.
- Run `git diff --check`.
- For config/rule/skill-only changes, state that app runtime tests were not run.
